 {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le18ob10re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Life's Uncertainties", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "  Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "  Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about timetables or schedules, you use the Simple Present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> By next week, we'll be friends again.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you going to let me in?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What are you doing here? \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I go to bed at 11:00.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about one action that will happen before another action in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous</span>, the action will have started in the future, but it will not be finished. It will be ongoing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I will be working at 4 p.m. tomorrow. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. <span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span> tense we often use a time marker to specify when something will have happened by.<br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We can leave until 10 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have picked</span> up the car by then.  <br/>The movie will start at 9 p.m. You will arrive at the theater at 9:15 p.m. When you arrive, the movie <span class=\"strong\">will have started</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The train will leave the station at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the station at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the train <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be going to/ will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> By next week, we will not <span class=\\\"strong\\\">be talking</span> about this.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have been</span> to the stars and back.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "By next week, we will not be talking about this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By this time on Friday, you girls are going to be swept away.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You will have been to the stars and back. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Friday, Vanessa will have truly understood the phrase paint the town red. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By this time next week, you are going to be asking everyone you know if you can borrow money.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "irrational ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not in accordance with reason", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is irrational right now. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to resolve a conflict between friends.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to kick out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to dismiss or eject forcefully from a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She kicked me out of her bar.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "annoyed, angry, upset", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She has every right to be heated with you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "face the music", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to face a difficult situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm glad you went over and faced the music.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take for granted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to assume someone or something will be available without asking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She feels like you took her and her friendship for granted.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mascot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person, animal, or object used as a symbol to represent a group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes I get tired of the two of you leading me around like a little puppy; like some team mascot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to blow out of proportion", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make more of a situation than it really is", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think Vanessa is blowing this way out of proportion.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "paint the town red", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go out and celebrate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa will have truly understood the phrase paint the town red. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine you work for a lifestyle magazine as a horoscope writer. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a future prediction for a classmate using future action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a prediction for this week, this month and this year.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use negatives in your predictions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about what your partner will be doing or what they will have done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make your predictions fun and always end with a positive prediction.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your predictions to the classmate you are writing about.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write future predictions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use Future tense, Future Perfect, Future Continuous in my predictions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present predictions clearly and effectively.", "type": "text"}]}]}